## AI Agent Instructions — SQL

When writing or reviewing SQL code in this project:

1. **Always enforce** SQL style guidelines
2. **Check column arrangement** follows the priority order (SKs → Non-SKs → Non-metrics → Metrics → Date → Timestamp)
3. **Verify** all reserved words and functions are UPPERCASE
4. **Ensure** proper indentation and line spacing
5. **Prefer CTEs** over subqueries
6. **Use descriptive aliases** with the `AS` keyword
7. **Format joins** with proper line breaks and indentation
8. **Never write `SELECT *`** — always enumerate every column explicitly, including inside CTEs, subqueries, and `QUALIFY` windows
9. **Always include a `WHERE` filter on partition or date columns** for partitioned or large tables to enable partition pruning; use `{load_start_date}` / `{load_end_date}` params for incremental loads and push filters into CTEs before joins
10. **Enforce Person Data Model** — in enrich and DW query files, never select raw PII columns (`name`, `email`, `phone`, `cpf`, `rg`, `address`, `dt_birth`) as stored columns; expose `sk_person` / `id_person` / `uuid_person` / `id_user` as foreign keys instead; consumers join `dw_public.dim_person` for contact details; in reverse DAG queries, always add a `has_right_to_be_forgotten = false` filter via `dim_person` before exporting any personal data

## SQL Style Checklist

- [ ] Columns are in English, lowercase, snake_case
- [ ] Columns arranged by priority
- [ ] All reserved words and functions are UPPERCASE
- [ ] Proper spacing around operators and commas
- [ ] New lines before AND/OR/ON, after SELECT/FROM/WHERE/JOIN
- [ ] Proper indentation (TAB or 2/4 spaces)
- [ ] Commas at end-of-line (right comma)
- [ ] Each column on its own row in SELECT
- [ ] No `SELECT *` — all columns enumerated explicitly (including inside CTEs, subqueries, and QUALIFY windows)
- [ ] CTEs used instead of subqueries
- [ ] Descriptive aliases with AS keyword
- [ ] Joins formatted with proper line breaks
- [ ] CASE-WHEN properly indented
- [ ] Comments formatted correctly (no blank lines)
- [ ] WHERE clause filters on partition/date columns for partitioned or large tables (enables partition pruning)
- [ ] Incremental loads use `{load_start_date}` / `{load_end_date}` params — no unbounded full scans
- [ ] Filters applied inside CTEs before joins rather than in the outermost query
- [ ] Enrich/DW tables use `sk_person` / `id_person` / `uuid_person` as FK — no raw PII columns (`name`/`email`/`phone`/`cpf`/`rg`/`address`) stored in enrich or DW tables
- [ ] Reverse DAG queries include a `has_right_to_be_forgotten = false` guard via `dim_person` before exporting any personal data to external systems
